('rwl1f_001', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The subway car was so ____ during rush hour that Leo could barely move his arms.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["empty", "silent", "tiny", "crowded"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'A place packed with so many people that it''s hard to move is crowded.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_002', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Aunt Rosa keeps her sewing room very ____. Every spool of thread sits in its own slot, and every piece of fabric is folded neatly on a shelf.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["noisy", "tidy", "dusty", "messy"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'A room where everything is folded and in its place is tidy.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_003', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The ____ dog waited by the front door every afternoon until its owner came home from work.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["loyal", "careless", "rude", "lazy"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'A dog that waits at the door every day for its owner is loyal.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_004', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Pronghorn are among the most ____ animals in North America. They can sprint away from predators at more than 50 miles per hour.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["clumsy", "heavy", "slow", "swift"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'An animal that can quickly outrun predators is swift.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_005', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Before his first speech in front of the whole school, Eli felt ____. His hands shook and his heart raced.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["proud", "nervous", "calm", "sleepy"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Shaking hands and a racing heart before a speech show that Eli was nervous.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_006', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Mrs. Diaz runs a small bakery on Elm Street. She orders the flour, plans the menu, and hires the staff.', null, 'As used in the text, what does the word "runs" most nearly mean?', '["manages", "flows", "races", "jogs"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Mrs. Diaz is in charge of the bakery, so "runs" means manages.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_007', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Baby sea turtles usually hatch at night. As soon as they dig out of the sand, they crawl toward the brightest part of the horizon. On a natural beach, that is the moonlit sky over the ocean, which leads them straight to the water.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To describe what adult sea turtles eat", "To explain how baby sea turtles find their way to the ocean", "To argue that beaches should be closed", "To compare sea turtles with land turtles"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text explains that hatchlings crawl toward the brighter horizon over the water.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_008', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Frogs and toads look alike, but they have several differences. Frogs usually have smooth, wet skin, while toads have dry, bumpy skin. Frogs have long legs for jumping, but toads have shorter legs for hopping. Frogs also tend to live near water, while toads can live in drier places.', null, 'Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?', '["It compares two similar animals by pointing out their differences", "It argues that toads make better pets", "It tells a story about a frog", "It lists the steps in a frog''s life cycle"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The text shows how frogs and toads differ in skin, legs, and habitat.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_009', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'The following text is from a short story.

Hana was awake an hour before her alarm went off. She had laid out her new backpack and shoes the night before. Today was her first day at a new school, and she couldn''t stop smiling as she pictured the art room she had seen on the tour.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To describe a school''s history", "To compare two different schools", "To show a character''s excitement at a new beginning", "To explain how to pack a lunch"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Hana wakes early and can''t wait to start her first day at a new school.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_010', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
Schools should give students a longer recess. Kids need time to run, play, and rest their minds.

Text 2
Researchers have found that students pay closer attention in class after they have had a break to play outside.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Text 1?', '["By agreeing and adding evidence that breaks help students focus", "By claiming that recess is too long already", "By saying that students don''t like recess", "By arguing that recess should be canceled"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 2''s research supports Text 1''s call for more recess.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_011', 'rw', 1, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
In the fall, the leaves of many trees turn yellow, orange, and red.

Text 2
Leaves are green because of a substance called chlorophyll. When days grow shorter in fall, trees stop making chlorophyll. As the green fades, other colors that were in the leaves all along begin to show.', null, 'Which choice best describes how the two texts are related?', '["Text 2 explains the cause of the change described in Text 1", "Text 2 disagrees with Text 1", "Both texts describe animals", "Text 1 explains Text 2"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 1 notes that leaves change color; Text 2 explains why.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_012', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Lonnie Johnson was an engineer who worked on spacecraft for NASA. At home, he was testing an idea for a cooling system when a nozzle he built shot a powerful stream of water across the room. That accident gave him the idea for the Super Soaker, which became one of the best-selling toys in the world.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Water guns were invented by NASA", "The toy failed to sell", "An engineer invented a famous toy while working on a different project", "Engineers should not make toys"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text tells how Johnson''s experiment with a cooling system led to the Super Soaker.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_013', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Capybaras, the world''s largest rodents, are famously calm. Birds often perch on their backs, and the capybaras don''t seem to mind. The birds are not just resting: they eat ticks and flies off the capybaras'' skin, which helps keep the big rodents free of pests.', null, 'According to the text, why do capybaras often have birds standing on their backs?', '["The birds help the capybaras find food", "The birds are resting during long flights", "The birds eat insects off the capybaras'' skin", "The capybaras carry the birds across rivers"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text says the birds pick bugs off the capybaras.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_014', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'The following text is from a short story.

After Grandpa moved to the city, Omar took over his garden. Every morning before school, he watered the tomatoes and checked the beans for beetles, just the way Grandpa had shown him. "I''ll keep it growing," he had promised, and he meant it.', null, 'Based on the text, how does Omar feel about his grandfather''s garden?', '["He values it and wants to take care of it", "He wants to replace it with a lawn", "He finds it boring", "He is afraid of the bees in it"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Omar waters the plants every day and promises to keep the garden growing.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_015', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Today, most people fly kites for fun. But kites have also done important work. Scientists once used kites to carry thermometers high into the sky to study weather. Engineers building a bridge over Niagara Falls in the 1840s used a kite to carry the first line across the gorge.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Kites were invented in the 1900s", "Kites have been used for many practical purposes, not only for fun", "Kites can fly only on windy days", "Kites are too dangerous to fly"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text lists scientific and engineering uses of kites.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_016', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'Four students took part in a summer reading challenge. A teacher claims that Jada read the most books.', '{"h": ["Student", "Books read"], "r": [["Jada", "14"], ["Ben", "9"], ["Lia", "11"], ["Max", "7"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the claim?', '["Lia read more books than Ben", "Four students took part in the challenge", "Ben read 9 books", "Jada read 14 books, more than any other student in the group"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The claim is that Jada read the most books; only this choice shows that.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_017', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a short story, Theo is described as a very patient person.', null, 'Which quotation from the story best shows that Theo is patient?', '["\"Theo lives near the edge of a forest.\"", "\"The deer had a white spot on its back.\"", "\"Theo waited quietly for over an hour until the shy deer finally stepped out of the woods.\"", "\"Theo wore a heavy brown jacket.\""]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Waiting quietly for an hour shows patience.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_018', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A coach claims that stretching before practice helps prevent injuries.', null, 'Which finding would best support the coach''s claim?', '["Players who stretched before every practice had fewer injuries during the season than players who did not", "The team won six games this season", "Stretching takes about ten minutes", "The team practices three times a week"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Only this finding links stretching to fewer injuries.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_019', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a poem, the speaker describes a winter storm as if it were a wild animal.', null, 'Which quotation from the poem best illustrates the claim?', '["\"We bought new boots at the store.\"", "\"My sister reads a book in bed.\"", "\"The kitchen clock says half past nine.\"", "\"The wind is a wolf that howls at my door, / and rattles the windows, and asks for more.\""]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'This quotation describes the wind as a wolf, comparing it to a wild animal.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_020', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'When Mia came home, the kitchen counter was dusted with flour, the oven was still warm, and the whole house smelled like cinnamon cookies. Mia guessed that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the oven had been broken for weeks", "nobody was home", "the house had no kitchen", "someone had been baking in the kitchen"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Flour, a warm oven, and the smell of cookies are clues that someone baked.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_021', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Dad heard a crash from the living room. When he ran in, he found pieces of a vase on the floor and the cat sitting on the high shelf right where the vase had been. He realized that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the dog had climbed onto the shelf", "the vase had been broken for years", "the cat had knocked the vase off the shelf", "a strong wind blew through the closed window"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The cat sitting on the shelf beside the broken vase is the clue.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_022', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'When Ana opened the curtains, the yard was covered in white, and the neighbors'' kids were already pulling sleds down the street. Ana guessed that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the school had closed for the year", "the sun was very hot", "it had probably snowed during the night", "it was the middle of summer"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A white yard and kids with sleds are signs of snow.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_023', 'rw', 1, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Kenji kept a bean plant on a table next to a sunny window. After two weeks, he noticed that its stem was leaning toward the glass. Kenji concluded that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the plant grew toward the light from the window", "the pot was too small", "someone had tied the plant to the window", "the plant did not need light"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Plants bend toward light, and this one leaned toward the sunny window.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_024', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'We had a picnic at the ____ ducks waddled over to beg for bread crumbs.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["park the", "park. The", "park and, the", "park, the"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'These are two complete sentences, so a period separates them.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_025', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'A rainbow has seven ____ orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["colors red,", "colors; red,", "colors: red,", "colors, red:"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A colon after a complete sentence introduces a list.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_026', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The soup was too ____ Liam blew on each spoonful before tasting it.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["hot; so,", "hot. So,", "hot, so", "hot so"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A comma comes before "so" when it joins two complete sentences.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_027', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The cookies in the ____ smell like chocolate and peanut butter.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["jar;", "jar,", "jar:", "jar"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'No punctuation belongs between the subject "The cookies in the jar" and the verb "smell."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_028', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The puppies in the basket ____ sleeping in a warm pile.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["was", "are", "is", "has been"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The subject "the puppies" is plural, so the verb is "are."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_029', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Grandpa showed us old photos from ____ trip to Mexico.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["its", "his", "her", "their"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The pronoun refers to "Grandpa," so "his" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_030', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Yesterday, my sister ____ a loaf of banana bread for the neighbors.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["baked", "bakes", "is baking", "will bake"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '"Yesterday" tells us the action happened in the past.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_031', 'rw', 1, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Three tiny ____ ran across the barn floor.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["mouses", "mices", "mice", "mouse''s"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The plural of "mouse" is "mice."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_032', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Most birds build nests in trees. ____ burrowing owls make their nests in holes in the ground.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["For example,", "However,", "Therefore,", "Also,"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The second sentence contrasts with the first.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_033', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'To plant a seed, first dig a small hole in the soil. ____ drop in the seed and cover it gently.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["For example,", "In contrast,", "However,", "Then,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The steps happen in order.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_034', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Fifty volunteers spent Saturday picking up litter along the shore. ____ the beach was clean by the afternoon.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["For instance,", "However,", "Instead,", "As a result,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The cleanup led to the beach being free of trash.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_035', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Mount Kilimanjaro is in Tanzania.
• It rises about 19,300 feet.
• It is the tallest mountain in Africa.
• It has snow near its top.
• Thousands of people climb it each year.', null, 'The student wants to describe the size of Mount Kilimanjaro. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Mount Kilimanjaro has snow near its top.", "Mount Kilimanjaro is in Tanzania.", "Thousands of people climb Mount Kilimanjaro each year.", "Mount Kilimanjaro rises about 19,300 feet, making it the tallest mountain in Africa."]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Only this choice tells how tall the mountain is.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl1f_036', 'rw', 1, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Bald eagles have white heads and brown bodies.
• They eat mostly fish.
• They build very large nests.
• In 1782, the bald eagle was chosen as the national bird of the United States.', null, 'The student wants to explain why the bald eagle is an important symbol. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Bald eagles have white heads.", "In 1782, the bald eagle was chosen as the national bird of the United States.", "Bald eagles eat mostly fish.", "Bald eagles build very large nests."]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Only this choice explains its role as a national symbol.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_001', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Coconut palms are remarkably ____. People use their fruit for food and oil, their leaves for roofing, and their trunks for building.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["useless", "versatile", "fragile", "outdated"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Something that can be used in many ways is versatile.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_002', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Although she had practiced for weeks, Amara was ____ to perform in front of the whole school; twice she asked her teacher whether someone else could go first.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["proud", "eager", "careless", "reluctant"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Someone who keeps asking to go later doesn''t want to perform; she is reluctant.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_003', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Sorting the thousands of seeds by size was ____ work: the students spent hours each day measuring them one at a time.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["thrilling", "effortless", "tedious", "brief"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Hours of slow, repetitive work are tedious.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_004', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The author''s descriptions are so ____ that readers feel as if they can see the bright market stalls and smell the spices.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["vivid", "dull", "vague", "brief"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Descriptions so clear that readers can almost see the scene are vivid.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_005', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The editor asked for a ____ report: no more than one page, with only the most important facts.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["confusing", "lengthy", "careless", "concise"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'A short report that still covers every important point is concise.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_006', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Experts studied the metal and the markings on the sword and confirmed that it was ____, made in the 1600s as the seller had claimed.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["damaged", "modern", "authentic", "fake"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A sword proven to be from the 1600s is genuine, or authentic.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_007', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'At its next meeting, the city council plans to address the flooding problem on River Road by discussing several ways to improve drainage.', null, 'As used in the text, what does the word "address" most nearly mean?', '["speak to", "locate", "write to", "deal with"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The council wants to solve the flooding problem, so "address" means deal with.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_008', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Beneath the town of Derinkuyu in Turkey lies an ancient city carved into soft volcanic rock. It extends at least eight levels down and could hold thousands of people, along with their animals and food. Historians believe residents built and used it as a place to hide during times of war.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To argue that people should live underground", "To compare several cities in Turkey", "To describe an underground city and explain why it was built", "To explain how caves form naturally"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text describes Derinkuyu and explains that it was built for shelter from attack.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_009', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'In 1935, about one hundred cane toads were brought to Australia to eat beetles that were damaging sugarcane crops. The toads did little to control the beetles. Instead, they spread across much of the continent, and their poison has killed many native animals that try to eat them.', null, 'Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?', '["It describes an action and then explains its unexpected harmful results", "It tells the life story of a scientist", "It compares two kinds of beetles", "It explains how sugarcane is harvested"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Cane toads were brought to control beetles but instead spread and harmed native wildlife.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_010', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Some animals have unusual adaptations to extreme cold. The Antarctic icefish, for instance, has no red blood cells at all; instead, its blood is clear. Scientists think the very cold, oxygen-rich water allows the fish to survive without them.', null, 'Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the overall structure of the text?', '["It introduces a new topic", "It contradicts the first sentence", "It states the author''s conclusion", "It gives an example that illustrates the claim in the first sentence"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The second sentence shows the ice fish as an example of an unusual adaptation.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_011', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'The following text is from a short story.

Rafael had been sure his first loaf would be a disaster. He slid it into the bakery''s display case and hid in the back. By noon, three customers had asked for "the bread with the crackly crust," and Rafael found himself standing a little taller behind the counter.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To explain why the character moved to a new city", "To describe how to bake bread", "To show how a character''s attitude changes after an unexpected success", "To compare two bakers"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Rafael starts doubtful but feels proud when customers praise his bread.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_012', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
Meat grown from animal cells in a laboratory could greatly reduce the environmental harm of farming. It would require far less land and water than raising cattle.

Text 2
Growing meat from cells requires large, carefully heated and cleaned facilities. If those facilities are powered mainly by fossil fuels, some studies suggest lab-grown meat could produce as much greenhouse gas as some kinds of beef.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Text 1?', '["By pointing out that the environmental benefits depend on how much energy the labs use", "By arguing that lab-grown meat tastes better", "By agreeing that lab-grown meat has no environmental costs", "By claiming that cattle produce no emissions"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 2 warns that the energy used by labs could reduce or cancel the benefits Text 1 describes.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_013', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
A writer claims that walking in a forest reduces stress in a way that no other activity can, because natural surroundings have a uniquely calming effect.

Text 2
In one study, people who walked on a treadmill indoors reported stress levels nearly as low as people who walked in a forest for the same amount of time. The researchers concluded that much of the benefit comes from physical activity itself.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the researchers in Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1?', '["By agreeing that walks in nature are the only way to reduce stress", "By arguing that the benefits come from exercise in general rather than from nature specifically", "By claiming that walking increases stress", "By arguing that city parks should be closed"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Text 2 found similar benefits from other exercise, challenging Text 1''s focus on nature.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_014', 'rw', 2, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
Settling Mars would give humanity a second home and push science and technology forward. Space agencies should make it a top priority.

Text 2
Mars has thin, unbreathable air and deadly radiation. The enormous sums needed to send people there would do far more good if spent on clean water, disease, and climate problems here on Earth.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Text 1?', '["By arguing that problems on Earth deserve more attention and funding than settling Mars", "By agreeing that Mars should be settled as soon as possible", "By arguing that space research has no value", "By claiming that Mars has plenty of breathable air"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 2 says money should first go to problems on Earth.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_015', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Born in 1867 to formerly enslaved parents, Madam C. J. Walker developed a line of hair-care products for Black women. She built a company that trained thousands of women as sales agents, giving them a way to earn their own income. By the time of her death in 1919, she was one of the most successful businesswomen in the United States.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Walker inherited a large fortune", "Walker turned her own hair-care products into a highly successful business that created jobs for many women", "Walker''s products sold poorly", "Walker worked only as a teacher"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text describes how Walker built a company and employed thousands of saleswomen.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_016', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Early light bulbs burned out quickly because their thin carbon filaments broke easily. In 1882, inventor Lewis Latimer patented a better way to make these filaments, which helped them last much longer and made electric lighting more practical. Latimer, the son of parents who had escaped slavery, was also a skilled draftsman who drew the plans for many inventions.', null, 'According to the text, what was Lewis Latimer''s contribution to the light bulb?', '["He invented the first light bulb", "He discovered electricity", "He found a way to make carbon filaments last longer", "He built the first power plant"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text says Latimer improved how carbon filaments were made so they lasted longer.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_017', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'The Great Pacific Garbage Patch is often imagined as a floating island of trash. In reality, much of it is made of tiny bits of broken-down plastic, many smaller than a grain of rice, spread through the water. From a boat, the ocean can look nearly clear, even where the plastic is most concentrated.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["The garbage patch is a solid island of trash", "Much of the plastic in the Great Pacific Garbage Patch is made of tiny pieces that are hard to see", "The garbage patch is found only near beaches", "Plastic in the ocean breaks down quickly"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The text corrects the idea of a floating island: most of the plastic is in tiny pieces.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_018', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'The following text is from a short story.

Dani had erased the same problem four times. Ms. Okoye didn''t say a word in front of the class. She just set a sticky note on Dani''s desk as she passed. It read: "Try drawing it first." Dani sketched the problem, and suddenly it made sense.', null, 'Based on the text, what is true about Ms. Okoye?', '["She is new to teaching", "She ignores students who make mistakes", "She notices when students are struggling and quietly helps them", "She dislikes teaching math"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'She sees Dani''s frustration and helps without embarrassing her.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_019', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Water-holding frogs live in the dry interior of Australia. When the land dries out, they burrow into the ground and wrap themselves in a waterproof layer of shed skin. They can stay buried for months or even years, emerging only after heavy rain fills temporary pools.', null, 'According to the text, how do some frogs survive in the desert?', '["They migrate to rivers each summer", "They store water in their eggs", "They stay buried underground until heavy rain falls", "They drink seawater"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The text says the frogs remain underground for months, coming out only after rain.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_020', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A student claims that the share of a town''s electricity produced by solar power more than quadrupled between 2015 and 2025.', '{"h": ["Source", "2015 (%)", "2025 (%)"], "r": [["Coal", "40", "15"], ["Natural gas", "35", "33"], ["Solar", "5", "22"], ["Wind", "20", "30"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the claim?', '["Solar''s share of the town''s electricity grew from 5 percent in 2015 to 22 percent in 2025", "The town used four energy sources", "Natural gas produced 33 percent in 2025", "Coal produced 40 percent of the town''s electricity in 2015"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The claim is that solar''s share more than quadrupled; 5 to 22 percent shows that.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_021', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a novel, the narrator describes how quickly her grandmother became an important member of a new community.', null, 'Which quotation from the novel most effectively illustrates the claim?', '["\"Grandmother greeted every stranger at the market by name within a week, and by the end of the month half the town came to her for advice.\"", "\"The market opened every Saturday morning.\"", "\"Grandmother moved to the town in the spring.\"", "\"Grandmother''s house had a blue door.\""]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Knowing everyone and being sought for advice shows how quickly she became part of the community.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_022', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A researcher hypothesizes that scrub jays remember where they hid their own seeds rather than simply searching every likely hiding spot.', null, 'Which finding, if true, would most directly support the researcher''s hypothesis?', '["Jays prefer acorns to pine seeds", "Jays found seeds they had hidden themselves far more often than seeds that researchers had hidden in similar spots", "Jays hide more seeds in the fall than in the spring", "Some hidden seeds sprout into new plants"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'If jays find their own hidden seeds better than others'' seeds, memory, not random searching, is at work.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_023', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'Four years after volunteers restored a wetland, the number of bird species there had more than doubled. The table shows that ____', '{"h": ["Year", "Bird species counted"], "r": [["1", "18"], ["2", "24"], ["3", "33"], ["5", "41"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?', '["24 species were counted in year 2", "more species were counted in year 3 than in year 2", "the number of species counted rose from 18 the first year to 41 four years later", "the survey was done each spring"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Only this choice shows the overall rise across the whole period.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_024', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A school district official claims that giving tablets to students caused a rise in test scores at several schools.', null, 'Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the claim?', '["The tablets were given to all fourth graders", "Teachers received training on the tablets", "Students used the tablets mostly for reading", "Test scores rose by a similar amount at schools in the district that did not get new tablets"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'If scores rose just as much without tablets, the tablets probably weren''t the cause.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_025', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a speech at a groundbreaking ceremony, the mayor argues that all children in the town should have easy access to a library.', null, 'Which quotation from the speech most effectively illustrates the claim?', '["\"The library will have three floors.\"", "\"Construction will begin in May.\"", "\"Every child in this town deserves a library within walking distance, and today we take the first step.\"", "\"I visited many libraries as a child.\""]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'This quotation expresses the belief that every child should have access to a library.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_026', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Under the floor of an ancient shop, archaeologists found a clay pot holding more than two hundred coins. All of the coins were minted during the years the shop is known to have been open. The pot had been carefully covered and hidden. The archaeologists concluded that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the coins were probably buried by the shop''s owner for safekeeping", "coins from that period were never used in trade", "the coins were dropped by tourists in recent years", "the shop was built on top of a modern bank"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Hidden under the floor of a shop and dated to when it operated, the coins were likely the owner''s stash.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_027', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Baby sea turtles can be confused by bright beach lights and crawl inland instead of toward the ocean. After a town replaced its beachfront lights with dim red ones that turtles have trouble seeing, the share of hatchlings heading the wrong way dropped sharply. This suggests that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["fewer turtles are nesting on the beach", "the lights cause hatchlings to crawl inland", "the new lights may be helping more hatchlings reach the sea", "the hatchlings prefer bright white light"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Fewer hatchlings went the wrong way after the lights changed.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_028', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'A diary entry dated April 18, 1906, describes being thrown out of bed by violent shaking, watching chimneys fall, and seeing smoke rise over the city''s downtown that same morning. Historians studying the diary suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the writer of the diary probably lived in the city in 1906", "the diary was written many years after the earthquake", "the writer had never visited the city", "the earthquake took place in another country"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The diary describes the shaking in detail on the day it happened, so the writer likely lived there.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_029', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'A student grew two groups of tomato plants in the same soil and gave both groups the same amount of water. Only one group received fertilizer. After a month, the fertilized plants were twice as tall. The results suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["water has no effect on plant growth", "both groups grew at exactly the same rate", "the plants were grown in different soil", "the fertilizer, not the extra water, likely caused the faster growth"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Both groups got the same water, and only the fertilized group grew faster.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_030', 'rw', 2, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Hikers crossing a dry valley noticed that the ground was covered with smooth, rounded stones, like those found in riverbeds. There is no river in the valley today. Geologists explain that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the valley has always been dry", "the river probably flowed through this valley long ago", "the stones were formed by a volcano", "the rocks were carried there by people"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Smooth, rounded river stones in a dry valley suggest a river once ran there.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_031', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The ancient city of Petra, in Jordan, was carved directly into red sandstone ____ buildings seem to glow pink at sunset.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["cliffs, its", "cliffs; its", "cliffs and its", "cliffs its"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Two complete sentences can be joined with a semicolon.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_032', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Gabriel García ____ Colombian novelist, won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1982.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["Márquez, a", "Márquez. A", "Márquez; a", "Márquez a"]'::jsonb, 0, null, '"a Colombian novelist" describes García Márquez and is set off by commas.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_033', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Inspectors at Ellis Island had several important ____ papers, examining health, and recording each arrival''s name.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["tasks, checking", "tasks: checking", "tasks checking", "tasks; checking"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'A colon after a complete sentence introduces the list.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_034', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Duke Kahanamoku was a famous Hawaiian ____ also won Olympic medals in swimming.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["surfer; who", "surfer who", "surfer. Who", "surfer, who"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '"who also won Olympic swimming medals" adds extra information about Duke Kahanamoku and is set off with a comma.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_035', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The okapis of the Congo rain ____ are close relatives of the giraffe.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["forest:", "forest", "forest,", "forest;"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'No punctuation belongs between the subject "The okapis of the Congo rain forest" and the verb "are."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_036', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The team of engineers working on the new bridge ____ finished the final design.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["are", "has", "were", "have"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The subject "the team" is singular, so "has" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_037', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The volunteers worked all day, and by sunset ____ had planted more than two hundred trees.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["she", "he", "it", "they"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '"The volunteers" is plural, so the pronoun is "they."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_038', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'If Lena keeps up her pace, by the end of the summer she ____ thirty books.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["read", "will have read", "has read", "had read"]'::jsonb, 1, null, '"By the end of the summer" points to a future deadline, so the future perfect is needed.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_039', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Reaching the top of the ridge, ____', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["the hikers saw a family of elk grazing in the meadow.", "the meadow had a family of elk grazing in it.", "a family of elk was seen grazing in the meadow.", "grazing in the meadow was a family of elk."]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The opening phrase describes who reached the ridge, so "the hikers" must come right after it.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_040', 'rw', 2, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The museum opened a new exhibit about the ____ soccer team that won the 1999 World Cup.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["womens", "woman''s", "women''s", "womens''"]'::jsonb, 2, null, '"Women" is already plural, so its possessive is "women''s."', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_041', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'A storm knocked down the rescue team''s radio tower. ____ the team kept searching through the night.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Similarly,", "Therefore,", "For example,", "Nevertheless,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The team kept going despite the storm, so a contrast fits.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_042', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Some plants get nutrients by trapping insects. ____ the pitcher plant lures insects into a slippery tube filled with digestive fluid.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Finally,", "However,", "For instance,", "In contrast,"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The second sentence gives an example of a plant that eats insects.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_043', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Many meadows where wild bees once fed have been turned into parking lots and lawns. ____ the number of wild bees in the region has dropped sharply.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Meanwhile,", "For example,", "Similarly,", "Consequently,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Losing their habitat led to fewer bees.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_044', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Bats find their prey in the dark by making sounds and listening for echoes. ____ dolphins use echoes to locate fish in murky water.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["However,", "Instead,", "Nevertheless,", "Likewise,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Both sentences describe animals that use the same strategy.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_045', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'To make maple syrup, workers collect sap from maple trees and pour it into large pans. They boil the sap for hours until most of the water evaporates. ____ they filter the thick syrup and pour it into bottles.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["In contrast,", "Finally,", "For example,", "However,"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The last step in the process comes after the others.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_046', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Angkor Wat is in Cambodia.
• It was built in the 1100s.
• It is the largest religious monument in the world.
• It covers about 400 acres.
• It was first a Hindu temple and later a Buddhist one.
• It appears on Cambodia''s flag.', null, 'The student wants to emphasize the size of Angkor Wat. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Angkor Wat, in Cambodia, is the largest religious monument in the world, covering about 400 acres.", "Angkor Wat appears on Cambodia''s flag.", "Angkor Wat was built in the 1100s.", "Angkor Wat was first a Hindu temple and later a Buddhist one."]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Only this choice emphasizes its size.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_047', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Marian Anderson was a famous American singer born in 1897.
• In 1939, she was refused permission to sing at a concert hall in Washington, D.C., because she was Black.
• Instead, she sang outdoors at the Lincoln Memorial.
• About 75,000 people came to hear her.
• In 1955, she became the first Black singer to perform with the Metropolitan Opera.', null, 'The student wants to describe Marian Anderson''s 1939 concert. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["In 1939, Marian Anderson sang outdoors at the Lincoln Memorial for a crowd of about 75,000 people.", "Marian Anderson was a famous American singer.", "In 1955, Marian Anderson performed with the Metropolitan Opera.", "Marian Anderson was born in 1897."]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Only this choice describes the 1939 concert.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_048', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Ellis Island is in New York Harbor.
• It opened as an immigration station in 1892.
• It closed in 1954.
• More than 12 million immigrants passed through it.
• It is now a museum.', null, 'The student wants to emphasize how many people passed through Ellis Island. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["More than 12 million immigrants passed through Ellis Island between 1892 and 1954.", "Ellis Island opened in 1892.", "Ellis Island is now a museum.", "Ellis Island is in New York Harbor."]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Only this choice gives the number of people.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_049', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Duke Kahanamoku was born in Honolulu in 1890.
• He won Olympic medals in swimming.
• He gave surfing demonstrations in Australia and California.
• These demonstrations helped spread surfing around the world.
• He later appeared in movies.', null, 'The student wants to explain why Duke Kahanamoku is important to the history of surfing. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Duke Kahanamoku was born in Honolulu in 1890.", "Duke Kahanamoku won Olympic medals in swimming.", "Duke Kahanamoku later appeared in movies.", "Duke Kahanamoku helped spread surfing around the world by giving demonstrations in places such as Australia and California."]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Only this choice explains his role in spreading surfing.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl2g_050', 'rw', 2, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• The okapi lives in the rain forests of central Africa.
• It is the giraffe''s closest living relative.
• It has striped legs like a zebra''s.
• It is shy and eats leaves.
• European scientists did not know about it until 1901.', null, 'The student wants to describe the okapi to an audience unfamiliar with it. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["The okapi was not known to European scientists until 1901.", "The okapi, a shy relative of the giraffe, lives in the rain forests of central Africa and has striped legs like a zebra''s.", "The okapi is shy.", "The okapi eats leaves."]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Only this choice gives a full picture of what an okapi is.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_001', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The theory connecting the two ancient cultures rests on a ____ link: a single word, found on one damaged tablet, that might or might not refer to the distant city.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["obvious", "robust", "tenuous", "documented"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A link based on a single ambiguous word is weak, or tenuous.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_002', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'In her memoir, the former senator is unusually ____ about her failures, describing in plain terms the policies she now believes were mistakes.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["flattering", "candid", "guarded", "rehearsed"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Openly admitting mistakes is being candid.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_003', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'To reconstruct the village''s history, the historian drew on ____ sources—diaries, tax records, ship logs, and even tree rings—that had never before been studied together.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["disparate", "identical", "obscure", "outdated"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Sources as different as diaries, tax records, and tree rings are disparate.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_004', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'The novel is ____ with references to Greek mythology: nearly every chapter alludes to a different god or hero.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["replete", "devoid", "wary", "independent"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'A novel full of references is replete with them.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_005', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Aware that early results are often overturned, the lead scientist was ____ in her public statements, describing the findings as "promising but preliminary."', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["boastful", "circumspect", "impulsive", "indifferent"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Careful, cautious statements are circumspect.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_006', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Words in Context', 'Although the first harvest from the new rice variety was impressive, agricultural experts urged farmers to temper their enthusiasm, noting that a single good season proves little.', null, 'As used in the text, what does the word "temper" most nearly mean?', '["harden", "moderate", "anger", "reveal"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Warning that the results might not last asks people to moderate their enthusiasm.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_007', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'Zitkála-Šá, a Yankton Dakota writer born in 1876, was sent as a child to a boarding school that discouraged Native languages and traditions. As an adult, she published collections of traditional Dakota stories in English and wrote essays describing her own experiences, ensuring that both the stories and the struggles of her community would reach a wide audience.', null, 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To describe how a writer used her work to preserve and share her people''s stories", "To argue that boarding schools improved education", "To summarize the plot of an opera", "To compare two Native American writers"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The text explains how Zitkála-Šá recorded Dakota stories and wrote about her own experiences.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_008', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'In 1908, an enormous explosion flattened about 80 million trees over a remote region of Siberia near the Tunguska River. Yet investigators who reached the site found no crater. Most researchers now conclude that a space rock exploded several miles above the ground, releasing its energy in the air before it could strike the surface.', null, 'Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?', '["It describes a mysterious event and then explains the explanation most researchers now accept", "It compares two similar explosions", "It describes the history of a Russian city", "It argues that the event never happened"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The text describes the Tunguska blast, notes the absence of a crater, and then gives the airburst explanation.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_009', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Text Structure and Purpose', 'In the 1930s, soil erosion was a serious problem across the southeastern United States. Officials encouraged farmers to plant kudzu, a fast-growing vine from Asia, to hold soil in place. With few natural enemies, the vine soon spread over fields, trees, and buildings, smothering native plants wherever it grew.', null, 'Which choice best describes the function of the third sentence in the overall structure of the text?', '["It argues that kudzu should be planted more widely", "It describes where kudzu first grew", "It explains how a solution to one problem created a new one", "It restates the main idea of the first sentence"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The third sentence shows that kudzu, planted to stop erosion, spread out of control.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_010', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
The traditional account of dog domestication holds that early humans deliberately captured wolf pups and raised them, gradually breeding the tamest animals to create dogs.

Text 2
Some researchers propose a different sequence. Wolves that were less fearful of people, they argue, began scavenging scraps near human camps on their own. Over many generations, these bolder wolves became a separate population, and only later did humans take an active role in shaping them.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the researchers described in Text 2 most likely respond to Text 1?', '["By arguing that wolves themselves began the process by choosing to live near humans", "By arguing that dogs were domesticated only recently", "By claiming that dogs did not descend from wolves", "By agreeing that humans captured and trained wild wolf pups"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'Text 2 suggests wolves domesticated themselves by scavenging near camps.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_011', 'rw', 3, 'Craft and Structure', 'Cross-Text Connections', 'Text 1
For decades, many archaeologists held that the first people in the Americas belonged to the Clovis culture, known for its distinctive stone spear points dating to about 13,000 years ago.

Text 2
At Monte Verde in Chile, researchers found remains of shelters, tools, and food that were reliably dated to about 14,500 years ago, more than a thousand years earlier than the oldest Clovis sites. Because Monte Verde lies far to the south, people must have arrived in the Americas earlier still.', null, 'Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the view described in Text 1?', '["By arguing that Monte Verde is younger than Clovis sites", "By agreeing that the Clovis people were the first Americans", "By claiming that no early sites have been found in South America", "By pointing to evidence that people were in the Americas before the Clovis culture"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Text 2 describes Monte Verde, which is older than Clovis, challenging Text 1''s view.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_012', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'For decades, physicists assumed that nature does not distinguish between left and right, a principle known as the conservation of parity. In 1956, two theorists suggested this might not hold for certain particle decays. Physicist Chien-Shiung Wu designed and led a demanding experiment with radioactive cobalt at extremely low temperatures, and her results showed clearly that parity is not conserved in such decays.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Wu designed experiments only in theory", "Wu won the Nobel Prize for her experiment", "Wu proved that the principle of parity was correct", "Wu''s carefully designed experiment overturned a widely accepted principle of physics"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The text emphasizes that Wu''s experiment disproved parity conservation.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_013', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'The following text is from a short story.

My father never said much when I left for college. He just filled my car''s gas tank, packed a cooler with sandwiches I hadn''t asked for, and checked the pressure in every tire twice. It was only halfway through the long drive, when I found the twenty-dollar bill tucked into the cooler lid, that I understood how much he had been trying to say.', null, 'Based on the text, what is true about the narrator''s father?', '["He has never driven before", "He is unhappy that the narrator is leaving", "He expresses his care through actions rather than words", "He speaks often about his feelings"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'He says little but fills the gas tank, packs food, and checks the tires.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_014', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'Slime molds are single-celled organisms with no brain. In one experiment, researchers placed oat flakes on a dish in a pattern matching the locations of cities around Tokyo and set a slime mold at the center. Within about a day, the slime mold had connected the oat flakes with a network of tubes strikingly similar to the region''s actual rail system.', null, 'According to the text, what did researchers observe about the slime mold?', '["It linked food sources with a network of tubes resembling a planned rail system", "It grew only toward the brightest light", "It avoided all the food sources", "It ate the oat flakes in random order"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The slime mold connected the oat flakes in a pattern similar to Tokyo''s railways.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_015', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Central Ideas and Details', 'At Chaco Canyon in present-day New Mexico, Ancestral Puebloan people built great stone houses between about 850 and 1150 CE. Researchers have found that several of these buildings are aligned with the rising and setting points of the Sun at the solstices and with the long cycle of the Moon''s movements, suggesting that astronomical observation guided their design.', null, 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["The Chaco Canyon buildings were built in random directions", "The people of Chaco Canyon had no interest in astronomy", "Chaco Canyon was abandoned before any buildings were made", "The buildings at Chaco Canyon appear to have been aligned with the movements of the Sun and Moon"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The text describes alignments of the buildings with solar and lunar cycles.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_016', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A researcher concluded that root fungi help tree seedlings grow, especially when the soil is low in nutrients.', '{"h": ["Soil type", "Growth with fungi (cm)", "Growth without fungi (cm)"], "r": [["Low-nutrient", "12.4", "5.1"], ["High-nutrient", "14.2", "13.0"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the researcher''s conclusion?', '["Two kinds of soil were used in the experiment", "Seedlings with fungi grew 14.2 centimeters in high-nutrient soil", "Seedlings with fungi grew 12.4 centimeters in low-nutrient soil, compared with 5.1 centimeters for those without fungi, while the difference in high-nutrient soil was much smaller", "Seedlings without fungi grew 13.0 centimeters in high-nutrient soil"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The conclusion is that fungi help most in poor soil; only this choice compares the gap in both soils.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_017', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'In a novel, the main character returns to her hometown with conflicted feelings, both resenting and missing it.', null, 'Which quotation from the novel most effectively illustrates the claim?', '["\"She arrived on the afternoon train.\"", "\"The town''s main street ran beside the river.\"", "\"She had sworn she would never come back to this town, yet every street corner seemed to call her by name.\"", "\"Her suitcase was old and scratched.\""]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'This quotation shows both her resistance to the town and its pull on her.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_018', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'Biologists hypothesize that a population of shrimp living near warm volcanic vents has inherited a greater tolerance for heat than a related population living in colder water.', null, 'Which finding, if true, would most directly support the hypothesis?', '["Both populations live in the same ocean", "The warmer-water population is larger than the colder population", "Shrimp in both populations eat the same algae", "Shrimp from the warmer-water population survived high temperatures much better than shrimp from the colder population when both were raised in identical conditions"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'If the difference persists when both are raised the same way, it is likely inherited.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_019', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'A food historian claims that a popular regional dish was invented at a particular restaurant when it opened in 1912.', null, 'Which finding, if true, would most directly weaken the historian''s claim?', '["Several letters describing the recipe were written decades before the restaurant opened", "The restaurant''s founder wrote a cookbook", "The dish became popular across the region in the 1920s", "The restaurant still serves the dish today"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'If the recipe existed before the restaurant, the restaurant didn''t invent it.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_020', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Command of Evidence', 'After a city opened a new light-rail line in 2020, officials said the line had drawn commuters out of their cars. Indeed, between 2018 and 2025, ____', '{"h": ["Way of commuting", "2018 (%)", "2025 (%)"], "r": [["Drive alone", "68", "58"], ["Public transit", "12", "19"], ["Bike", "4", "7"], ["Walk", "6", "6"]]}'::jsonb, 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?', '["the share of commuters who walked was 6 percent in 2025", "the share of commuters using public transit rose from 12 percent to 19 percent, while the share driving alone fell from 68 percent to 58 percent", "four ways of commuting were measured", "the share of commuters who biked rose from 4 to 7 percent"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Only this choice shows transit rising while solo driving fell, matching the statement.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_021', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Cave paintings in southern France show woolly rhinoceroses and cave lions with features, such as body shape and fur patterns, that match frozen remains of these extinct animals found much later in Siberia. These details suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the animals shown in the paintings never existed", "the paintings were likely made by artists who had seen the animals alive", "the paintings were made after the animals went extinct", "the paintings were copied from later books"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'Accurate details of extinct animals suggest the painters observed them directly.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_022', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'After wind turbines were built on a ridge, local residents blamed them for a decline in the region''s songbirds. But surveys show that songbird numbers fell by a similar percentage over the same years in nearby valleys that have no turbines. These findings suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["wind turbines are harmless to every species", "the turbines caused all of the decline", "the songbirds have moved to the mountain", "the decline in the songbird population is unlikely to be explained by the new wind turbines alone"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'Songbirds declined just as much in areas without turbines, so turbines can''t explain it alone.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_023', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'A medieval manuscript of unknown origin uses an ink made from a recipe recorded only in one monastery''s documents, and its handwriting matches that of a scribe named in the monastery''s records. Scholars therefore suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the ink was made after the monastery closed", "the monks bought all their books from other cities", "the manuscript was written on modern paper", "the manuscript was probably copied in the monastery''s own scriptorium"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The manuscript''s ink and handwriting match the monastery''s own records.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_024', 'rw', 3, 'Information and Ideas', 'Inferences', 'Researchers recorded faint sounds coming from inside turtle eggs shortly before hatching. Eggs kept in contact with other eggs tended to hatch within hours of one another, while eggs kept separate hatched over several days. These results suggest that ____', null, 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["the eggs hatch only in complete silence", "the eggs hatch at random times", "the eggs may be using sound to time their hatching together", "turtles cannot hear at all"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Eggs that heard their siblings hatched together; isolated eggs did not.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_025', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Signed in ____ Antarctic Treaty set aside the continent for peaceful scientific research.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["1959 the", "1959; the", "1959. The", "1959, the"]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'The introductory phrase "Signed in 1959" is followed by a comma.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_026', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'Darwin''s notebooks record a crucial ____ the finches on different islands had beaks of different shapes, each suited to the food available there.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["observation", "observation;", "observation:", "observation,"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'A colon introduces the explanation of what the observation was.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_027', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The exhibition explores the influence of Japanese printmakers such as Utagawa ____ prints inspired Van Gogh and Monet—on European painting.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["Hiroshige; whose", "Hiroshige—whose", "Hiroshige, whose", "Hiroshige whose"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The interruption ends with a dash, so it must begin with one.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_028', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Boundaries', 'The probe was designed to operate for only ninety days in ____ it continued sending data for more than fourteen years.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["space, however,", "space however,", "space, however", "space; however,"]'::jsonb, 3, null, '"However" joins two complete sentences, so a semicolon comes before it and a comma after.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_029', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'The origin of the humpback whale''s complex songs, which can last for hours and change from year to year, ____ a subject of intense study.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["have remained", "remains", "are remaining", "remain"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The subject is the singular "origin," not "songs," so "remains" is correct.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_030', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'By the time the team made its discovery in 2019, the lead researcher ____ the glacier for nearly two decades.', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["had been studying", "is studying", "studies", "will study"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The studying began before the past event (the discovery) and continued up to it.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_031', 'rw', 3, 'Standard English Conventions', 'Form, Structure, and Sense', 'Listening through hydrophones for three straight nights, ____', null, 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["the species sang a song that the researchers recorded.", "the researchers recorded a song never before heard from the species.", "recording the song was done by the researchers.", "a song never before heard from the species was recorded."]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The opening phrase describes who listened through the night, so "the researchers" must come right after it.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_032', 'rw', 3, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'Adding new roads to reduce traffic seems like a straightforward solution. ____ studies have found that new roads often increase traffic, because they encourage more people to drive.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Paradoxically,", "Similarly,", "Therefore,", "For example,"]'::jsonb, 0, null, 'The result is the opposite of what one would expect.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_033', 'rw', 3, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'The species is endemic to the island. ____ it is found nowhere else on Earth.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Nevertheless,", "Meanwhile,", "In other words,", "In contrast,"]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'The second sentence restates the first in simpler terms.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_034', 'rw', 3, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Transitions', 'The pollen preserved in the lake sediment shifts abruptly from tree species to grasses around 4,000 years ago. ____ the surrounding forest likely gave way to open grassland at about that time.', null, 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["For instance,", "Thus,", "Conversely,", "Still,"]'::jsonb, 1, null, 'The conclusion follows from the evidence in the first sentence.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_035', 'rw', 3, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• The Antarctic Treaty was signed in 1959.
• It was first signed by twelve countries.
• It reserves Antarctica for peaceful purposes and scientific research.
• It bans military activity on the continent.
• More than fifty countries have now joined it.', null, 'The student wants to explain the treaty''s main purpose. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["The Antarctic Treaty was signed in 1959.", "More than fifty countries have now joined the Antarctic Treaty.", "The Antarctic Treaty reserves the continent for peaceful purposes and scientific research, banning military activity.", "The Antarctic Treaty was first signed by twelve countries."]'::jsonb, 2, null, 'Only this choice explains what the treaty is for.', 'published', 'import', now()),
('rwl3f_036', 'rw', 3, 'Expression of Ideas', 'Rhetorical Synthesis', 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• The mirror test checks whether an animal recognizes its own reflection.
• Magpies are members of the crow family.
• Researchers placed a small colored mark on each magpie''s throat feathers, where the bird could see it only in a mirror.
• Several magpies repeatedly tried to remove the mark while looking in the mirror.
• The researchers concluded that magpies, like great apes and dolphins, can recognize themselves.', null, 'The student wants to present the study''s conclusion to an audience already familiar with the mirror test. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Researchers placed a small colored mark on each magpie''s throat feathers.", "Magpies are members of the crow family.", "The mirror test checks whether an animal recognizes its own reflection.", "The results suggest that magpies, like great apes and dolphins, can recognize themselves in a mirror."]'::jsonb, 3, null, 'This audience already knows the test, so the best choice goes straight to the conclusion.', 'published', 'import', now())
on conflict (id) do nothing;
